{
  "name": "ORYVIA",
  "description": "ORYVIA is a local browser-based workstation for phenotype-genotype association and posterior effect analysis, with applications in plant quantitative genetics. It aligns phenotype and genotype matrices, imports tabular and VCF data, runs GLM and mixed-model association scans, and supports native rMVP FarmCPU when R dependencies are installed. Single-trait empirical Bayes and multivariate mash workflows estimate adjusted effects and uncertainty. Candidate review retains trait units, genotype coding, carrier support and sensitivity information. Optional reference annotations and dosage-based linkage disequilibrium support interval-to-gene lookup. Manhattan, quantile-quantile, effect-interval and response plots can be exported with source data and settings. Computation runs on the user's computer through a browser interface on Windows, macOS or Linux; synthetic examples and input templates are included.",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/YueDong0211/ORYVIA",
